usage: cairn measure [-h] [--db PATH] [--bundle PATH] [--pin PATH]
                     [--attest PATH] [--log LEVEL] [--json]
                     [--sizes BITS,BITS,...] [--seeds N] [--cap-ops N]
                     [--cap-minutes M]
                     [{toy-curve-tries,rho60}]

measure a skill's cost constant (toy-curve-tries: tries and subprocess wall
over seeds 1..N per size; rho60: interpreted Pollard rho rate at 60 bits with
a completed 40-bit rho)

positional arguments:
  {toy-curve-tries,rho60}
                        what to measure

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --db PATH             substrate SQLite file
  --bundle PATH         gate bundle SQLite file
  --pin PATH            gate-bundle pin file
  --attest PATH         attestation file
  --log LEVEL           log level for the JSON records on stderr
  --json, --robot       emit exactly one JSON document on stdout
  --sizes BITS,BITS,...
                        bit sizes to measure
  --seeds N             seeds 1..N per size
  --cap-ops N           rho60: stop the 60-bit walk after N group ops
  --cap-minutes M       rho60: stop the 60-bit walk after M minutes

Structured output: add --json to any read-side command. Contract: cairn
capabilities --json. Agent handbook: cairn robot-docs.
